From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] aggregation: a copied observation is not an independent
 source

Reviewer finding 2, reproduced against the real service and broker: a second
agent's byte-identical copy of a note counted as an extra agent and root, so
min_agents = 3 was met by 2 genuine sources. compose_rule now treats active
raw notes with the same slot and the same text (case and whitespace
normalised) as one source; the earliest observation (then store arrival
order, which replay keeps) stands for it. Paraphrases are not detected.

Not changed: a verbatim re-post of a RETRACTED note by another agent still
counts. The golden scenario follows_evidence (steps 36-41) specifies exactly
that recount as evidence; blocking it would contradict the reference, so it
is left as an owners' decision (reviewer finding 3).

tests/copied_roots.rs fails before (copied_roots.rs:49: the copy completed
the conclusion) and passes after, with an independent-observation control.
Goldens, datapath and golden_scenarios pass.

